From: meanaverage <18336095+meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:44:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] feat(web): microphone redirection (AUDIO_INPUT) through
 an `audioInput` callback

The web client could not redirect a microphone. With the new
`audioInput(callback)` extension, it advertises audio capture
(INFO_AUDIOCAPTURE) and listens for the AUDIO_INPUT dynamic channel
([MS-RDPEAI]) with `ironrdp-rdpeai`'s client, offering 16-bit PCM at 48,
44.1, 22.05 and 16 kHz, mono and stereo. The browser captures, so the
backend only tells the callback what the server asked for:
`{ type: 'open', sampleRate, channels }` when capture should start (or
switch format) and `{ type: 'close' }` when it should stop. JavaScript
pushes interleaved 16-bit PCM back with `audioInputData(samples)`
through `invokeExtension`, in any length; it is cut into the packet size
the server asked for, and dropped while no capture is open.

Servers open the channel when a remote application starts recording and
close it when it stops (Windows, and GNOME Remote Desktop, which opens
it while something records from its PipeWire source), so a listener
creates a fresh client for each opening rather than registering one
channel once.

The Open PDU's capture format only sets the packet length in frames;
Data PDUs carry the negotiated encoding format. GNOME Remote Desktop
describes 44.1 kHz stereo as WAVE_FORMAT_EXTENSIBLE there, which the
backend accepts.

[MS-RDPEAI]: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/windows_protocols/ms-rdpeai/
